  "question": "Given $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$$ calculate $(AB)C$ and $A(BC)$ and verify that they are equal.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "<b>Product $AB$</b><br>$$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Evaluation of $(AB)C$</b><br>$$(AB)C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 3 \\\\ -13 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Product $BC$</b><br>$$BC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Evaluation of $A(BC)$</b><br>$$A(BC)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 3 \\\\ -13 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Hence, $(AB)C=A(BC)$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
